<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="page legaldoc">
  <h1>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Effective <%= co.EFFECTIVE_DATE %> · Applies to all use of <%= co.PRODUCT_NAME %></p>

  <h2>Cancellation / stopping use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There is <b>no contract and no automatic charge</b>. You can stop using the software at any time without notice. Months with no usage produce no invoice.</li>
    <li>Invoices are issued on the 1st of the month for the previous month's actual usage and are due within 15 days. If an invoice remains unpaid after the due date, we may suspend your account until it is paid.</li>
    <li>To close your account permanently, email us<% if (co.COMPANY_EMAIL) { %> at <a href="mailto:<%= co.COMPANY_EMAIL %>"><%= co.COMPANY_EMAIL %></a><% } %>. We will close the account and delete your data in line with our Privacy Policy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Usage fees</b> cover work the software has already completed and are therefore <b>non-refundable</b>, except where the software recorded usage incorrectly (for example double counting). In that case we correct the invoice before payment, or refund the difference in full if already paid.</li>
    <li><b>Software not working:</b> if the software does not work with your e-WorkPermit account as described on this website and we cannot fix the problem within 5 business days of your report, we refund the usage fees for the affected month in full, or void the invoice if it has not yet been paid.</li>
    <li><b>Disputed amounts:</b> report any discrepancy within 15 days of the invoice date. We verify against the usage log (visible in your customer portal) and correct the invoice before payment.</li>
    <li><b>Duplicate or erroneous charges</b> are always refunded in full.</li>
    <li>No refunds are given for: a suspended or non-working e-WorkPermit account on your side, decisions made by government authorities, or government fees — these are not our charges.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Email <% if (co.COMPANY_EMAIL) { %><a href="mailto:<%= co.COMPANY_EMAIL %>"><%= co.COMPANY_EMAIL %></a><% } else { %>our support address<% } %> with the email used at checkout, the invoice number (INV-…) or Lemon Squeezy order number, and the reason.</li>
    <li>We reply within 2 business days. Approved refunds are issued through Lemon Squeezy to the original payment method within 5–10 business days, depending on your card issuer.</li>
    <li>You may also contact Lemon Squeezy directly via the links in your receipt email; as Merchant of Record it may process refunds under its <a href="https://lemonsqueezy.com/buyer-terms" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Buyer Terms</a>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Chargebacks</h2>
  <p>Please contact us before disputing a charge with your bank. We resolve most issues within 2 business days.</p>
</section>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
